      "section_title": "Guarding the city and registering the returnees",
      "text": "After the wall is built and the gates are set in place, Nehemiah appoints trustworthy leaders and establishes watches for Jerusalem. Because the city is large but sparsely populated, he gathers the nobles, rulers, and people for registration and reads the record of those who first returned from captivity. The chapter then lists families, priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, temple servants, possessions, gifts, and the cities where the people settle.",
